(1269942, 161269, 35044, '<td valign="top">Great picture - nicely taken.<br/> <br/>Only criticism is in choice of book version, as collected works means that we see a lot of pages on LHS: doesn''t imply "beginning".  Also, while I agree that prologue is the right place to emphasise, it comes halfway down page of text - again, slightly off the beginning topic.  <br/> <br/>Overall, though, very nice pic.</td>', 'Great picture - nicely taken. Only criticism is in choice of book version, as collected works means that we see a lot of pages on LHS: doesn''t imply "beginning".  Also, while I agree that prologue is the right place to emphasise, it comes halfway down page of text - again, slightly off the beginning topic.   Overall, though, very nice pic.', '2005-04-04 11:37:31.000000', NULL, 1),
(1269944, 161083, 7689, '<td valign="top">it''s your picture and composition... ver nice... I would have preferred the shot with coffee in the cup and beans spread around.</td>', 'it''s your picture and composition... ver nice... I would have preferred the shot with coffee in the cup and beans spread around.', '2005-04-04 11:37:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(1269945, 160744, 7689, '<td valign="top">my only 10</td>', 'my only 10', '2005-04-04 11:38:37.000000', NULL, 1),
(1269947, 160966, 35044, '<td valign="top">there are a couple of other cload shots in the challenge the b&amp;w one does this better (I think) but yours is better than most of the others.  Perhaps not quite dramatic enough here.  Sky could grade faster to darker blue (increased contrast would help) and clouds do not seem to have a very white colour at thier whitest - a levels tweak would help that.  Compositionally, a bit more cloud or a bit more sky (depending on which is more interesting) with possible adherence to the rule of thirds would improve the image, I think.</td>', 'there are a couple of other cload shots in the challenge the b&w one does this better (I think) but yours is better than most of the others.  Perhaps not quite dramatic enough here.  Sky could grade faster to darker blue (increased contrast would help) and clouds do not seem to have a very white colour at thier whitest - a levels tweak would help that.  Compositionally, a bit more cloud or a bit more sky (depending on which is more interesting) with possible adherence to the rule of thirds would improve the image, I think.', '2005-04-04 11:39:45.000000', NULL, 1),
