(1273506, 161319, 20018, '<td valign="top">well, I liked it. It was my first post of a psuedo macro-shot.  I used two primes (50mm/1.8 and a 35mm/2) nose to nose to get extremely close to my wife''s eye. Unfortunately, since I was handholding I couldn''t stop down enough and the DOF was probably less than 1mm; therefore the reason for all of the "blurry" type comments.  I used a small penlight to light up the area just behind her eye.  The idea was to have a "sunrise" or dawn over her eye...but ended up not being able to execute it on short notice. Ah well, maybe I''ll try it later with a tripod and less giggly subject (I think she had too much wine :).<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-06 09:35:03.</i></td>', 'well, I liked it. It was my first post of a psuedo macro-shot.  I used two primes (50mm/1.8 and a 35mm/2) nose to nose to get extremely close to my wife''s eye. Unfortunately, since I was handholding I couldn''t stop down enough and the DOF was probably less than 1mm; therefore the reason for all of the "blurry" type comments.  I used a small penlight to light up the area just behind her eye.  The idea was to have a "sunrise" or dawn over her eye...but ended up not being able to execute it on short notice. Ah well, maybe I''ll try it later with a tripod and less giggly subject (I think she had too much wine :).', '2005-04-06 01:13:19.000000', '2005-04-06 10:35:03.000000', 0),
