(1286106, 161018, 28299, '<td valign="top">I get the feeling that the "controversial" comment might be from someone who is not English-speaking (no country listed). I had a hard time deciphering that "sentence" without any punctuation. When I did understand it, I felt the person was just making a comment in general,  not judging you. Photographers take "controversial" photos all the time; it doesn''t mean it''s THEIR personal belief system. I don''t believe in killing, but I''d probably take a photograph of a victim (and then puke - LOL)!<br/>BTW - beautiful photo. I didn''t vote in that challenge.<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2005-04-12 17:02:13.</i></td>', 'I get the feeling that the "controversial" comment might be from someone who is not English-speaking (no country listed). I had a hard time deciphering that "sentence" without any punctuation. When I did understand it, I felt the person was just making a comment in general,  not judging you. Photographers take "controversial" photos all the time; it doesn''t mean it''s THEIR personal belief system. I don''t believe in killing, but I''d probably take a photograph of a victim (and then puke - LOL)!BTW - beautiful photo. I didn''t vote in that challenge.', '2005-04-12 18:01:04.000000', '2005-04-12 18:02:13.000000', 0),
